//! The no-infra OAuth2 scope rig. Generated by CIaC (`26UpdatePlan.md`
//! M4). A real RS256 keypair, served from a real in-process JWKS stub
//! built on `axum` -- the same dependency `crate::auth::Jwks` already
//! uses to fetch JWKS in production -- so `Claims::from_request_parts`
//! runs its actual code path: fetch JWKS, match `kid`, verify a real
//! signature, check `iss`/`aud`/`exp`.
//!
//! **Embedded, not generated, keypair** (Open question 2's own
//! per-target accommodation, disclosed): `jsonwebtoken`'s RS256 support
//! is backed by `ring`, which deliberately does not expose RSA key
//! generation (a documented `ring` design choice, not an oversight) --
//! adding a keygen dependency here just to mint an ephemeral test key
//! would be a heavier dependency cost than embedding one, so this file
//! embeds a fixed 2048-bit test keypair instead, used by no other
//! target and only for signing throwaway tokens minted and verified in
//! this file alone.

